f, which included the defending gold medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/12558"} "Rodrigo Pessoa"] " of Brazil. He rode cleanly in the jump-off, but so did American " [:a {:href "/athletes/107020"} "Beezie Madden"] " and German " [:a {:href "/athletes/116730"} "Meredith Michaels-Beerbaum"] ", with Madden winning the bronze medal on time, 35.25 to 35.37 for Michaels-Beerbaum. Pessoa took 37.04 to complete his jump-off round and seemed to finish fifth, but he would be disqualified when his horse, " [:a {:href "/horses/show/2894"} [:em {} "Rufus"]] " tested positive for nonivamide, a drug similar to capsaicin, and used for its anti-inflammatory properties. Several other riders were also disqualified in this event, all for using topical anti-inflammatory medications on their horses."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Faults"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "315"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/116707"} "Eric Lamaze"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2821"} "Hickstead"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "4 (=1)"] [:td {} "0 (=1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "381"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11609"} "Rolf-Göran Bengtsson"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2859"} "Ninja"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "8 (=6)"] [:td {} "0 (=1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""